WEBVTT

00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:13,720
the phone on my right bulb is moved towards the center.

00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:15,720
Uh-huh.

00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,720
And I'm wondering how to remedy that situation.

00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:22,720
Sure. So you have the two rubber caps on either end.

00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,720
This happens very often.

00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:25,720
Okay.

00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:29,720
So if you just pull the rubber end off where the foam is starting to fall in,

00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,720
grab a needle nose pliers,

00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:36,720
you should be able to grasp the end of that foam from the needle nose pliers

00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:39,720
and pull that towards the edge.

00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:44,720
Once it reaches the edge, what I've told people is if they wanted to take a single dab of

00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:50,720
a gorilla glue or, you know, super glue and just do one little dot

00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:56,720
at the very end of that tube on the inside and then press the foam up into that.

00:00:56,720 --> 00:01:01,720
It should dry fairly quick and it will just hold that little spot in place.

00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:05,720
So it's less likely to break away and slip down towards the center.

00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:06,720
Okay. Great.

